`grep -rn find_triple_backtick . --exclude-dir={node_modules,.git,target,.svelte-kit,dist,build,.scratch,tasks}` → exactly 3 hits, all in src-tauri/src/vault/parsing.rs: :942, :948 (call sites) and :967 (private definition). No other surface.

`awk 'NR>=900&&NR<=990' src-tauri/src/vault/parsing.rs` — the fn is:
```
967 fn find_triple_backtick(bytes: &[u8], start: usize) -> Option<usize> {
968 \tif bytes.len() < 3 { return None; }
971 \tlet mut i = start;
972 \twhile i + 2 < bytes.len() {
973 \t\tif bytes[i]==b'`' && bytes[i+1]==b'`' && bytes[i+2]==b'`' { return Some(i); }
976 \t\ti += 1;
978 \tNone
979 }
```
Line accounting: doc 964-966 (3) + fn 967-979 (13) = **16** — the audit's -16 is right; but the finding *title* says "14-line manual byte loop" and the body is 13 lines.

Edge cases, checked against the primary replacement `content[start..].find("```").map(|i| i + start)`:
- Buffer end: last valid i is len-3 (`i+2 < len`); `find` also matches a triple ending at the last byte. Same.
- 4+ backticks: "````" → both return 0; the follow-up search from `after_open=3` sees only one backtick → both None. "``````" → both open 0, close 3. Same.
- Short buffer: `bytes.len() < 3` guard vs `find` on a <3-byte haystack → both None.
- `start == len`: reachable, since `after_open = open_idx + 3` and `open_idx <= len-3`. `&content[len..]` is the valid empty slice → None; the manual loop also returns None. No panic.
- `start > len`: manual returns None, `content[start..]` **panics**. Unreachable here — the outer loop guard at :940 is `while search_from + 3 <= bytes.len()` and `search_from = close_end = close_idx + 3 <= len`.
- Char boundary: every `start` is 0, `open_idx+3`, or `close_idx+3`, and all three of those bytes are backticks (ASCII), so slicing is boundary-safe. `content` is in scope: `pub fn strip_non_body_content(content: &str)` at :918, `bytes = content.as_bytes()` at :919.

`grep -rn strip_non_body_content src-tauri/src src-tauri/tests` → 2 production callers (vault/index.rs:129, :700) plus 20+ assertions in parsing.rs's own test module (:2371-2530). No test touches `find_triple_backtick` directly.

No rustfmt.toml anywhere (`find . -maxdepth 2 -name 'rustfmt.toml'` → empty) and `grep -rn 'cargo fmt|clippy' .github/ scripts/ package.json` → no hits, so the slightly longer call-site lines are not gated by any formatter.
